What is StatefulSet+PV+PVC ---> Called as Static Provisioning ?

StatefulSet is used for database pods where PersistanceVolume(PV) is used to define the desired volume based on our requirement we
define and we can retain it with the help of  policy and Storage Class is used for dynamic volume as per user requirement request PersistanceVolumeCliam(PVC) is used to connect
the PersistanceVolume(PV) to StatefulSet pods

Example: 1. PersistentVolume (PV).yaml


apiVersion: v1                                                                       
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: mysql-pv-0
  labels:
    app: pv-0
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 5Gi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain
  hostPath:
    path: "/mnt/data0"



or 
Example: 1. PersistentVolume (PV).yaml  in AWS EBS

apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: ebs-static-pv
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 5Gi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain
  storageClassName: ""
  awsElasticBlockStore:
    volumeID: vol-0a1b2c3d4e5f6g7h8   # <-- tumhara real volumeID yahan aayega
    fsType: ext4




Example: 2. PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC).yaml


apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: mysql-pvc
  labels:                               ------------------> this is foir if we are using databse deployment not stafulsets
    app: mysql
spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 5Gi
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: mysql




Examole: 3. StatefulSet (StatefulSet.yaml)


apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: StatefulSet
metadata:
  name: mysql
spec:
  serviceName: "mysql"
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: mysql
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: mysql
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: mysql
          image: mysql:5.7
          env:
            - name: MYSQL_DATABASE
              valueFrom:
                configMapKeyRef:
                   name: mysql-configmaps
                   key: database
            - name: MYSQL_USERNAME
              valueFrom:
                secretKeyRef:
                   name: mysql-secrets
                   key: username
            - name: MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD
              valueFrom:
                secretKeyRef:
                   name: mysql-secrets
                   key: password
          ports:
            - containerPort: 3306
          volumeMounts:
            - name: mysql-pvc-0
              mountPath: "/var/lib/mysql"

  volumeClaimTemplates:
    - metadata:
        name: mysql-pvc-0
      spec:
        accessModes:
          - ReadWriteOnce
        resources:
          requests:
            storage: 5Gi
        selector:
          matchLabels:
            app: pv-0
